        "merged_at": "2025-07-21T21:37:15Z"
      },
      "body": "## Description\r\n\r\n[ What changed? Feel free to be brief. ]\r\n\r\nEdit mode was changed months ago but never updated in the docs. https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/5801\r\n\r\nI updated the Edit feature documentation to reflect that it's now only accessible via\r\n  Cmd+I (no longer through a mode selector), removing all references to the old VS Code\r\n  Edit mode interface and updating keyboard shortcut formatting. I also replaced the Edit\r\n  demonstration gif in the getting-started overview and added an image to the\r\n  how-to-customize page to show the model selection interface.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I've read the [contributing guide](https://github.com/continuedev/continue/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] The relevant docs, if any, have been updated or created\r\n- [x] The relevant tests, if any, have been updated or created\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\n[ For visual changes, include screenshots. Screen recordings are particularly helpful, and appreciated! ]\r\n\r\n![edit](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ac2b566-c658-440e-945c-ecf0c4ce6a74)\r\n\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n[ What tests were added or updated to ensure the changes work as expected? ]\r\n\n    \n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n\n## Summary by cubic\nUpdated the Edit feature documentation to show that Edit is now only accessible with Cmd+I or Ctrl+I, removing all references to the old mode selector and updating shortcut formatting.\n\n- **Docs Updates**\n  - Replaced outdated instructions and images.\n  - Added a new image for model selection in Edit.\n  - Updated the Edit demonstration gif.\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n",
